---
// About benchmarks.law: who keeps the bench, how to contribute, where to reach him.
// Contact details are the ones arthur.law/contact publishes.
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site
	title="About"
	current="about"
	description="Who keeps benchmarks.law, how to add a tool, send a document or challenge a score, and where to reach Arthur Souza Rodrigues."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="page-head">
			<p class="eyebrow">About<span class="sep">·</span>benchmarks.law</p>
			<h1>Open benchmarks for legal documents. Come build them.</h1>
			<p>
				benchmarks.law measures how faithfully DOCX tools reproduce Microsoft Word, and how legal AI tools hold up
				against in-house lawyers. Every input, output, score and log is published, so any number here can be checked,
				reproduced or challenged.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<section id="who">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2 class="sec-label"><span class="sq"></span> / Who keeps it</h2>
			<div class="about-body">
				<p>
					I'm Arthur Souza Rodrigues, a lawyer working between New York and São Paulo on contracts, legal operations and
					legal AI. I started the bench because lawyers live in Word, and the tools that promise to handle Word
					documents are rarely measured against Word itself.
				</p>
				<p>
					Full disclosure: I also write jubarte, one of the engines compared here. That is why the scorer is lifted
					verbatim from an independent benchmark, every vendor runs on the same fixed document sets, and the leaderboard
					marks no tool as ours.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="contribute">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2 class="sec-label"><span class="sq"></span> / Contribute</h2>
			<div class="hl-grid">
				<div class="work-item">
					<span class="tag">Tools</span>
					<h3>Add a tool</h3>
					<p>If it converts DOCX to PDF or compares two documents without a GUI, it can be benchmarked. Open an issue with how to run it.</p>
					<a class="go" href="https://github.com/jandira-tech/neurotic_docx_bench/issues" rel="noopener">Open an issue →</a>
				</div>
				<div class="work-item">
					<span class="tag">Documents</span>
					<h3>Send a document that breaks things</h3>
					<p>The fixtures are real documents. One that trips Word, an engine or the scorer is worth more than a hundred that don't.</p>
					<a class="go" href="https://github.com/jandira-tech/neurotic_docx_bench/issues" rel="noopener">Report it →</a>
				</div>
				<div class="work-item">
					<span class="tag">Scores</span>
					<h3>Challenge a score</h3>
					<p>Think a number is wrong, or the method is unfair to a tool? Link the case and say why. Corrections land in the changelog.</p>
					<a class="go" href="https://github.com/jandira-tech/neurotic_docx_bench" rel="noopener">Read the method →</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="contact" id="reach">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2 class="sec-label"><span class="sq"></span> / Get in touch</h2>
			<h2>Using these numbers, building a tool, or just curious? Say hello.</h2>
			<p>
				Add me on LinkedIn, follow the work on GitHub and Hugging Face, or write directly. For consulting and legal
				work, the contact page has the details and a booking link.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/arthrod" rel="noopener">Connect on LinkedIn <span class="arr">→</span></a>
				<a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://arthur.law/contact" rel="noopener">Contact page</a>
			</div>
			<dl class="facts">
				<div class="fact"><dt>Email</dt><dd><a href="mailto:contact@arthur.law">contact@arthur.law</a></dd></div>
				<div class="fact"><dt>Based</dt><dd>New York · São Paulo</dd></div>
				<div class="fact"><dt>GitHub</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/arthrod" rel="noopener">github.com/arthrod</a></dd></div>
				<div class="fact"><dt>Hugging Face</dt><dd><a href="https://huggingface.co/arthrod" rel="noopener">huggingface.co/arthrod</a></dd></div>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>
</Site>
